  "name": "Agung ensembles (Lumad hanging-gong music of Mindanao)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ensembles of large suspended bossed gongs (agung) among non-Muslim Mindanao peoples such as the Bagobo, Manobo and Tiruray (Teduray), in which several players each sound one or two gongs in interlocking patterns, sometimes with a drum, for rituals, festivities and dances. They differ from the kulintang tradition, which leads with a row of small gongs. The gong card (bossed) stands in for the agung.",
